    \(5.00\)
  \item
    \(3.33\)
  \item
    \(0.40\)
  \item
    \(0.80\)
  \end{enumerate}

  \textbf{Solution}\\
  Pelas propriedades das funções de densidade, temos que
  \[\begin{aligned}
  1&=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} f(x) dx  \\
  & = \int_{-\infty}^{0}\!\! 0 dx + \int_0^{0.4}\!\! Cx dx + \int_{0.4}^1\!\! 3.33(1-x) dx + \int_{1}^{\infty}\!\! 0 dx \\
  & = C \int_0^{0.4}\!\! x dx + 3.33 \int_{0.4}^1\!\! (1-x) dx \\
  & = C \left[ \frac{x^2}{2} \right]_0^{0.4} + 3.33 \left[ x- \frac{x^2}{2} \right]_{0.4}^1 \\
  & = C \frac{0.16}{2} + 3.33 \left(1 - \frac{1}{2} - 0.4 + \frac{0.16}{2}\right) \\
  & = 0.08 C + 0.5994.
  \end{aligned}\] Resolvendo-se em \(C\), obtemos \(C=5\).

